  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the key uncertainty is whether a well-designed multimodal, multiprofile configuration can establish a strong performance ceiling and inform which design axes (RNA encoder, image encoder, aggregation, fusion) matter most. config_010 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion) is a balanced, near-optimal starting point: it combines both modalities (most likely to outperform single-modality), uses multiprofile with transformer aggregation (best for integrating multiple profiles), and uses weighted fusion (flexible modality combination). It avoids the most expensive choices (ViT-L, scGPT) to keep cost moderate (~2-3x a single-modality PCA baseline in GPU hours), preserving budget for 9 follow-up experiments that can test whether upgrading the image encoder to ViT-L or the RNA encoder to scGPT/scVI yields meaningful gains. This gives a strong reference accuracy and simultaneously tests the core hypothesis that multimodal + multiprofile + transformer aggregation is the right architectural backbone."
}

